            docs-only work; dialog and bottom sheet are planned for 0.4.
            Prereq: repo pushed to GitHub.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>0.3.0</strong></td>
        <td>Forms</td>
        <td>✅ Checkbox, radio, switch, styled native select, text-field
            variants (filled, error/helper, textarea), button
            disabled/active states — first library growth since 0.1, driven
            by docs needs. Zero JS forms; semantic <code>--fl-error</code>
            token precedes theming.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>0.4.0</strong></td>
        <td>Feedback &amp; containment</td>
        <td>✅ Dialog (five M2 types, non-dismissible opt-out), bottom
            sheet (modal + standard, 50dvh cap, grid contents, no drag
            handle), snackbar (one at a time, 4s auto-dismiss), progress
            (linear + circular, zero JS), tooltip (CSS-only, four
            directions) — plus the forms-completion pass: field
            architecture rebuilt (box owns the chrome), affixes, icons,
            counter, password toggle, valid-HTML label contract.
            "Overlay" retired as a concept.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>0.5.0</strong></td>
        <td>Data display + app chrome</td>
        <td>Data table, standalone tabs, pagination, avatar, chips (split
            from badges) — plus the app-chrome set that enables a
            Keep-style app build: <strong>menu</strong>
            (dropdown on the native Popover API — light-dismiss, Escape,
            instant dismiss — deferred here from 0.4),
            <strong>top app bar</strong> promoted to a component
            (own docs page, safe-area top inset, action ordering,
            scroll-hide, contextual action bar state,
            <strong>transparent variant</strong> with search-in-bar —
            Google's actual web pattern;
            extended/prominent/dense/images-in-bar deliberately
            discarded — mobile-first native feel), <strong>checkbox-driven
            selection state</strong> on list rows, <strong>side
            sheet</strong> (standard + modal, completes the sheet family;
            audit against a <code>sheets-side-docs/</code> reference
            folder before building), docs recipes (empty state, card
            grid). Master-detail split: <strong>not in 0.5</strong> — M2
            has no spec, Google's own web apps are inconsistent (Gmail =
            split, Keep/Drive = overlay); returns in a later release as
            an "App shells" guide composed from existing primitives,
            sequenced after the side sheet. <strong>Acceptance: the notes
            prototype (<code>prototype/test-mdl2.html</code>) rebuilt
            entirely on Flint components in the Keep-web form factor
            (rail on desktop, editor as centered dialog) as the first
            <code>samples/</code> entry — zero hand-rolled chrome; only
            the app logic (data, undo) is author code.</strong></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>0.6.0</strong></td>
        <td>Theming</td>
